w: By His bit- ter grief and woe He saved us from the e- vil foe.
w: Gives His bo- dy with the bread And with the wine the blood He shed.
w: For if he does not be- lieve, Then death for life he shall re- ceive.
w: And, to mend what we have done, Gave in- to death His on- ly Son.
w: By the sick who are dis- tressed, By hearts that long for peace and rest.
w: Art thou well? A- void this board, Else thou rea- pest an ill re- ward.
w: They who feel no want nor ill Need no phy- si- cian's help nor skill.
w: This feast is not spread for thee If thine own sa- vior thou wilt be.
w: His dear guest thou here shalt be, And Christ Him- self shall ban- quet thee.
w: That true love let him re- ceive, Which here to thee thy God doth give.
